-- title:
--   Residue of a cusp-regular integral function is w-integral
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and an integer $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of the field $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_{M'} =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions) with residue field target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`; thus $R_0$ consists of a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue map onto that field with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ on constants, a map on places preserving degrees and orders, and a normalisation clause. Assume the compatibility hypothesis `hR₀`: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-coefficients lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, and suppose its coefficientwise image $\hat g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and is cusp-regular: for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, $\hat g$ also has non-negative order. Let $w$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ which is rational, i.e. the structure map to its residue field is surjective, and suppose the generator `jGeomGen (ResidueField A) M'` lies in the valuation subring of $w$. Then $R_0$'s residue of $\hat g$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$.
--
--   This is the statement that a function regular on the affine integral model of the level-$M'$ modular curve reduces to a function regular on the affine special fibre at $q$: $R_0$-integrality together with regularity away from the poles of the $j$-generator forces the reduction to be integral at every place of the special-fibre function field where the reduced $j$-generator is. It is used in the analysis of special fibres at full level, for instance in locating places under maximal ideals of the $j$-chart and in the identification of moduli points with Tate points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_residue_mem_toValuationSubring_of_cuspRegular_of_isRational.lean

